WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.521
Initial handling can influence what evidence remains available and how defensible the case is later.

2
00:00:06.521 --> 00:00:11.374
Before interacting with an iPhone, document the device condition as found.

3
00:00:11.374 --> 00:00:23.810
Record the physical state, power state, lock state, visible notifications, network indicators, connected accessories, SIM or eSIM context at a high level, and any damage or unusual condition.

4
00:00:23.810 --> 00:00:28.663
Photographs and notes create a record that later reviewers can understand.

5
00:00:28.663 --> 00:00:32.075
Lock state and power state are especially important.

6
00:00:32.075 --> 00:00:40.417
A powered-on, unlocked, recently unlocked, or locked device may present different evidence opportunities and different risks.

7
00:00:40.417 --> 00:00:48.758
A device that has not been unlocked after restart may expose less data through lawful tools than one that has already been unlocked.

8
00:00:48.758 --> 00:00:56.265
The point is not to defeat the lock state; the point is to document it and understand how it shapes acquisition options.

9
00:00:56.265 --> 00:01:01.800
Network isolation may be appropriate in some situations, but it should be deliberate.

10
00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:08.852
Investigators may need to prevent remote changes, new messages, sync updates, or device management actions.

11
00:01:08.852 --> 00:01:15.222
At the same time, changing network state can alter evidence conditions or affect running services.

12
00:01:15.222 --> 00:01:21.212
The decision should follow policy, authority, case needs, and documentation requirements.

13
00:01:21.212 --> 00:01:26.748
Chain of custody records who handled the device, when, why, and under what conditions.

14
00:01:26.748 --> 00:01:35.165
It should capture transfers, storage, examination activity, acquisition actions, and any material change in the evidence state.

15
00:01:35.165 --> 00:01:42.672
This record helps establish that evidence was controlled and that any unavoidable changes were known and explained.

16
00:01:42.672 --> 00:01:45.781
Avoid unnecessary interaction with the device.

17
00:01:45.781 --> 00:01:55.563
Swiping through screens, opening applications, changing settings, or dismissing notifications can create new artifacts and alter existing context.

18
00:01:55.563 --> 00:02:00.264
Early handling should be careful, minimal, authorized, and documented.

19
00:02:00.264 --> 00:02:07.619
Those first choices can affect what is available later, so preservation discipline is part of the evidence itself.
